1
00:00:00,013 --> 00:00:01,614
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,616 --> 00:00:03,020
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,104 --> 00:00:05,133
(Episode 90)

4
00:00:07,005 --> 00:00:08,805
- I'm home.
- Ji Hu.

5
00:00:08,845 --> 00:00:10,014
Come sit here for a minute.

6
00:00:10,118 --> 00:00:12,881
Let me check on Ji Ni first.
I haven't heard from her all day.

7
00:00:13,365 --> 00:00:15,633
Just sit down. She's not in her room.

8
00:00:19,592 --> 00:00:20,592
Where did she go?

9
00:00:21,851 --> 00:00:23,138
Did you know about this?

10
00:00:23,505 --> 00:00:25,174
Did you two discuss divorce?

11
00:00:25,327 --> 00:00:26,327
Divorce?

12
00:00:30,942 --> 00:00:32,094
What is this?

13
00:00:32,795 --> 00:00:33,795
Divorce?

14
00:00:34,592 --> 00:00:35,598
Did Ji Ni give you this?

15
00:00:35,678 --> 00:00:36,863
Where is Ji Ni now?

16
00:00:37,502 --> 00:00:38,798
I told you, she's not upstairs.

17
00:00:38,885 --> 00:00:39,898
Calm down and listen.

18
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,453
How can I be calm right now?

19
00:00:42,991 --> 00:00:45,476
- How is this possible?
- So you knew nothing about this?

20
00:00:45,578 --> 00:00:46,880
Ji Ni did this on her own?

21
00:00:47,028 --> 00:00:48,120
Why would Ji Ni do that?

22
00:00:49,405 --> 00:00:52,378
We were struggling,
but our marriage was fine.

23
00:00:52,434 --> 00:00:55,520
We haven't even had a proper talk
since she left the hospital.

24
00:00:55,845 --> 00:00:58,832
Right. You barely saw her.
You didn't get to talk either.

25
00:00:59,112 --> 00:01:00,205
What did I tell you?

26
00:01:00,492 --> 00:01:02,132
She did this on her own.

27
00:01:03,578 --> 00:01:06,310
That's how she is. Cold and heartless.

28
00:01:09,157 --> 00:01:12,046
Mom, what did you say to Ji Ni?

29
00:01:12,146 --> 00:01:13,678
Here he goes, blaming me again.

30
00:01:13,712 --> 00:01:15,158
What could I have said?

31
00:01:15,305 --> 00:01:17,034
I was going to bring her herbal tonic.

32
00:01:17,258 --> 00:01:19,172
Then she put this right in front of me.

33
00:01:19,708 --> 00:01:20,764
She said she'd had enough.

34
00:01:20,978 --> 00:01:23,855
She was tired of hurting you
and being miserable herself.

35
00:01:23,857 --> 00:01:25,154
She just wanted to leave.

36
00:01:26,795 --> 00:01:27,795
Is that true?

37
00:01:29,451 --> 00:01:31,030
I tried to calm her down.

38
00:01:31,345 --> 00:01:33,175
I said, "You can't do this."

39
00:01:33,325 --> 00:01:37,338
"Married couples stick together
through good times and bad."

40
00:01:38,065 --> 00:01:39,518
Let's be fair.

41
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:43,630
Did your dad or I ever give her
a dirty look over the miscarriage?

42
00:01:43,735 --> 00:01:45,842
We treated her like a queen.

43
00:01:46,429 --> 00:01:47,984
I can't believe this.

44
00:01:48,537 --> 00:01:49,537
That makes no sense.

45
00:02:23,391 --> 00:02:27,698
The phone you are calling is turned off.
You will now be connected to voicemail.

46
00:02:32,192 --> 00:02:33,749
Jung A, where are you? Let's meet.

47
00:02:35,338 --> 00:02:36,338
I'll come to the studio.

48
00:02:43,684 --> 00:02:45,843
Ji Hu's coming? Why?

49
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:47,833
I don't know.

50
00:02:48,591 --> 00:02:49,816
Why do you keep coming here?

51
00:02:49,818 --> 00:02:51,265
You should go home after work.

52
00:02:52,098 --> 00:02:53,787
I come here because I'm upset.

53
00:02:53,801 --> 00:02:55,037
What's upsetting you?

54
00:02:55,969 --> 00:02:57,755
- Is it about Ji Ni?
- Aren't you upset too?

55
00:02:57,831 --> 00:02:59,755
Are you happy
while your friend's struggling?

56
00:03:01,095 --> 00:03:02,345
Who said I was happy?

57
00:03:04,345 --> 00:03:05,592
I'm upset too.

58
00:03:05,938 --> 00:03:07,176
So just go, please.

59
00:03:07,178 --> 00:03:09,772
Ji Ni's married. Stop worrying about her.

60
00:03:10,452 --> 00:03:12,963
What's the point of meeting?
We're both in unrequited love.

61
00:03:12,969 --> 00:03:13,969
Unrequited love?

62
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:15,591
Wasn't that all in the past?

63
00:03:17,425 --> 00:03:18,729
Do you still like Ji Hu?

64
00:03:19,196 --> 00:03:20,196
Enough!

65
00:03:22,991 --> 00:03:24,709
Mom, I'm going to see Jung A.

66
00:03:25,017 --> 00:03:26,017
Jung A?

67
00:03:26,198 --> 00:03:28,449
Yes, good idea. You should ask her.

68
00:03:28,705 --> 00:03:29,705
Okay.

69
00:03:31,118 --> 00:03:32,507
The hotel yesterday was a bad idea.

70
00:03:32,573 --> 00:03:33,846
You went to a hotel yesterday?

71
00:03:33,848 --> 00:03:36,009
He kept moving from room to room
to avoid Ji Ni,

72
00:03:36,010 --> 00:03:37,609
so I felt bad and took him there.

73
00:03:37,611 --> 00:03:38,878
I think that was a mistake.

74
00:03:40,085 --> 00:03:43,380
As Mom said, she has no family home.
I wanted to give Ji Ni space to rest.

75
00:03:44,061 --> 00:03:46,938
But I should've been home with her,
even if I slept in the living room.

76
00:03:47,332 --> 00:03:48,456
I didn't think it through.

77
00:03:49,045 --> 00:03:51,150
- That's true.
- What do you mean?

78
00:03:51,152 --> 00:03:52,412
She's not a child.

79
00:03:52,712 --> 00:03:54,010
Anyway, I'll be back.

80
00:03:54,345 --> 00:03:56,145
Please answer your phone, just in case.

81
00:04:00,005 --> 00:04:01,252
This is so upsetting.

82
00:04:08,932 --> 00:04:10,756
Hide well.

83
00:04:11,214 --> 00:04:12,798
Don't let anyone find you.

84
00:04:26,405 --> 00:04:27,405
Jung A.

85
00:04:27,915 --> 00:04:28,915
You're here too?

86
00:04:29,358 --> 00:04:30,444
Yes. What is it now?

87
00:04:32,038 --> 00:04:33,445
Ji Ni left home.

88
00:04:34,238 --> 00:04:35,294
She only left divorce papers.

89
00:04:35,989 --> 00:04:37,699
- What?
- Divorce papers?

90
00:04:37,825 --> 00:04:39,733
How could she do that without telling you?

91
00:04:43,449 --> 00:04:47,447
Actually, I did see Ji Ni.

92
00:04:47,502 --> 00:04:49,105
Really? She came here?

93
00:04:49,538 --> 00:04:50,918
She seemed to be struggling.

94
00:04:51,472 --> 00:04:52,949
She said she was exhausted,

95
00:04:53,123 --> 00:04:55,668
so I listened and talked to her,
like I always do.

96
00:04:55,816 --> 00:04:57,427
And? Did she say anything else?

97
00:04:57,652 --> 00:04:59,092
Did anything seem different?

98
00:04:59,831 --> 00:05:01,195
You should've called me right away.

99
00:05:01,892 --> 00:05:02,892
Well...

100
00:05:03,059 --> 00:05:05,608
Out of nowhere, she asked me
to take good care of you.

101
00:05:05,809 --> 00:05:07,885
She said, "Please," then rushed out.

102
00:05:08,485 --> 00:05:10,431
I thought she just wanted me...

103
00:05:10,432 --> 00:05:12,338
to look after you and your mom,
like last time.

104
00:05:16,872 --> 00:05:19,904
I had no idea she was planning
to leave home.

105
00:05:20,225 --> 00:05:21,225
Where would she go?

106
00:05:21,718 --> 00:05:23,216
Tell me if you have any idea.

107
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:24,949
I'm not sure.

108
00:05:26,258 --> 00:05:27,678
Was there a letter or anything?

109
00:05:28,385 --> 00:05:31,098
I was in a hurry, so I barely looked.
But no, there wasn't one.

110
00:05:31,265 --> 00:05:34,278
She left divorce papers.
Why would she leave a letter?

111
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:36,351
That's why there must be some message.

112
00:05:37,291 --> 00:05:38,352
Go home and look.

113
00:05:38,798 --> 00:05:41,472
And make sure her mom
and the family in Seo Chon know.

114
00:05:42,645 --> 00:05:44,505
I'll call her mom.

115
00:05:45,245 --> 00:05:46,245
I'll do it.

116
00:05:47,264 --> 00:05:48,264
But...

117
00:05:48,778 --> 00:05:49,778
What?

118
00:05:50,618 --> 00:05:52,418
Give Ji Ni some time.

119
00:05:53,745 --> 00:05:56,271
She really likes being alone.

120
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:59,044
She hates being disturbed
when she's on her own.

121
00:05:59,221 --> 00:06:01,020
If she left the papers,

122
00:06:01,022 --> 00:06:03,269
shouldn't we assume it's what she wants?

123
00:06:03,418 --> 00:06:05,885
She left divorce papers!
How can he not look for her?

124
00:06:07,678 --> 00:06:09,960
This could be her way of asking for help.

125
00:06:10,156 --> 00:06:11,210
She's really struggling.

126
00:06:12,211 --> 00:06:15,690
You should've stayed home after a fight.
Why go to a hotel?

127
00:06:16,952 --> 00:06:18,235
I already regret it.

128
00:06:19,332 --> 00:06:20,966
I'll check with both families.

129
00:06:21,355 --> 00:06:22,355
Thanks.

130
00:06:31,965 --> 00:06:32,965
What?

131
00:06:33,414 --> 00:06:34,414
Why keep staring?

132
00:06:34,895 --> 00:06:36,724
Do you think I'm lying?

133
00:06:36,872 --> 00:06:39,346
You can't lie when someone's watching you.

134
00:06:41,171 --> 00:06:42,171
Just go.

135
00:06:42,265 --> 00:06:44,147
I'll close up and go home too.

136
00:06:44,379 --> 00:06:46,676
Then let's go. I'll drive you home.

137
00:06:46,736 --> 00:06:47,736
No, thanks.

138
00:06:47,896 --> 00:06:49,582
I'll go alone. Don't worry about me.

139
00:06:49,584 --> 00:06:51,105
Do whatever you like.

140
00:06:59,605 --> 00:07:00,605
Seriously...

141
00:07:04,565 --> 00:07:06,321
Aunt, it's me, Ji Hu.

142
00:07:07,528 --> 00:07:10,027
Ji Hu? Is that you?

143
00:07:13,593 --> 00:07:14,593
Aunt.

144
00:07:17,852 --> 00:07:20,693
I was about to ring the bell,
but I heard your voice.

145
00:07:20,783 --> 00:07:23,392
Good. What's going on?

146
00:07:24,718 --> 00:07:26,089
Is Ji Ni here, by any chance?

147
00:07:27,309 --> 00:07:28,309
Ji Ni?

148
00:07:29,583 --> 00:07:32,827
She stopped by earlier, then left. Why?

149
00:07:32,855 --> 00:07:34,405
Earlier? When?

150
00:07:34,465 --> 00:07:37,783
About two hours ago? Maybe three?

151
00:07:38,977 --> 00:07:41,358
Why? Didn't she go home?

152
00:07:46,892 --> 00:07:48,029
Divorce papers?

153
00:07:48,522 --> 00:07:49,522
Yes.

154
00:07:49,958 --> 00:07:52,118
She gave Mom divorce papers and left.

155
00:07:52,685 --> 00:07:53,728
That's impossible.

156
00:07:54,718 --> 00:07:56,714
Why did she come here? What did she say?

157
00:07:56,807 --> 00:07:58,503
Did you notice anything unusual?

158
00:07:59,458 --> 00:08:01,624
She said she wanted to apologize...

159
00:08:01,950 --> 00:08:04,725
because her mom wouldn't,
so she did it for her and left.

160
00:08:05,044 --> 00:08:06,323
Unbelievable...

161
00:08:06,358 --> 00:08:08,284
Maybe she went to her mom to apologize?

162
00:08:08,786 --> 00:08:09,805
I'll go check.

163
00:08:10,978 --> 00:08:12,998
Please let me know if she contacts you.

164
00:08:13,532 --> 00:08:14,532
Ji Hu.

165
00:08:14,779 --> 00:08:16,691
Did anything happen at home?

166
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:18,205
No.

167
00:08:18,672 --> 00:08:20,149
Mom and Dad both treated her well.

168
00:08:20,458 --> 00:08:21,926
If she'd planned to leave,

169
00:08:22,247 --> 00:08:23,991
she'd have gone somewhere no one knows.

170
00:08:25,538 --> 00:08:28,381
I'm most worried she might hurt herself.

171
00:08:29,238 --> 00:08:32,011
No, she wouldn't. She's sensible.

172
00:08:33,618 --> 00:08:36,647
So when she visited earlier,
she'd already decided to leave.

173
00:08:39,435 --> 00:08:40,587
I'll check with her mom.

174
00:08:47,055 --> 00:08:48,456
What can we do about this?

175
00:09:02,131 --> 00:09:03,831
Who is it?

176
00:09:04,529 --> 00:09:05,631
Mother, it's me.

177
00:09:20,091 --> 00:09:22,525
Why are you here so late?
I told you not to come.

178
00:09:23,492 --> 00:09:25,798
Did something happen to Ji Ni?
What's wrong?

179
00:09:26,392 --> 00:09:27,814
So Ji Ni hasn't been here?

180
00:09:28,183 --> 00:09:29,912
She hasn't contacted you?
I gave her your number.

181
00:09:29,978 --> 00:09:32,458
That girl is way too stubborn
to come here.

182
00:09:33,372 --> 00:09:34,872
What brings you here so late at night?

183
00:09:36,053 --> 00:09:37,153
Did...

184
00:09:37,657 --> 00:09:40,011
Lee Cheol go looking for Ji Ni?

185
00:09:40,252 --> 00:09:41,363
Hurry up and tell me.

186
00:09:41,643 --> 00:09:42,643
No.

187
00:09:43,658 --> 00:09:45,175
Ji Ni left the house.

188
00:09:45,741 --> 00:09:47,108
She left the divorce papers behind.

189
00:09:47,794 --> 00:09:49,498
What? She left?

190
00:09:50,074 --> 00:09:52,805
Where could she possibly go?

191
00:09:54,524 --> 00:09:55,524
What on earth...

192
00:09:56,199 --> 00:09:58,810
Did you ask her to divorce you?

193
00:09:58,811 --> 00:10:00,503
Why would I do that?

194
00:10:00,714 --> 00:10:02,358
Then why did she leave?

195
00:10:02,359 --> 00:10:03,654
What did you do to her?

196
00:10:03,656 --> 00:10:05,026
This is because of you, Mother.

197
00:10:05,725 --> 00:10:06,870
Before she left,

198
00:10:06,872 --> 00:10:08,718
she went to Seo Chon,
got on her knees, and begged.

199
00:10:09,332 --> 00:10:10,933
Since you refused to apologize,

200
00:10:10,934 --> 00:10:12,530
she went and apologized on your behalf.

201
00:10:13,712 --> 00:10:16,136
Why does Ji Ni always have to
keep her head down?

202
00:10:16,458 --> 00:10:18,025
It's all your fault, Mother!

203
00:10:19,317 --> 00:10:20,317
Ji Hu.

204
00:10:20,352 --> 00:10:22,135
Why did you have to cause
all this trouble?

205
00:10:24,752 --> 00:10:26,103
If that incident had never happened...

206
00:10:28,055 --> 00:10:29,150
Ji Ni...

207
00:10:29,709 --> 00:10:31,205
gets anxious whenever she's happy.

208
00:10:31,932 --> 00:10:34,785
She can't even enjoy a moment of peace.
Do you know how heartbreaking that is?

209
00:10:34,787 --> 00:10:36,696
That's why I cut ties with her.

210
00:10:36,925 --> 00:10:39,371
I stepped aside so you two
could be happy together!

211
00:10:40,412 --> 00:10:41,978
Didn't your mom drive her away?

212
00:10:42,187 --> 00:10:45,311
She gave Yeong Ju a hard time too.
Did you think she'd leave Ji Ni alone?

213
00:10:45,624 --> 00:10:46,858
Go ask your mom.

214
00:10:46,872 --> 00:10:49,735
Mom has been treating Ji Ni well lately.

215
00:10:49,737 --> 00:10:50,880
So have I!

216
00:10:50,998 --> 00:10:53,292
I've already backed off completely.

217
00:10:53,378 --> 00:10:56,025
What more do you want from me?
Should I die?

218
00:10:57,613 --> 00:10:58,613
Forget it.

219
00:11:00,965 --> 00:11:01,965
I'm sorry.

220
00:11:02,490 --> 00:11:03,716
I'll look for her again tomorrow.

221
00:11:04,483 --> 00:11:05,879
Ji Hu.

222
00:11:07,425 --> 00:11:08,858
Don't sign the divorce papers.

223
00:11:09,336 --> 00:11:11,233
Get rid of them, okay?

224
00:11:12,252 --> 00:11:13,404
I'm never getting divorced.

225
00:11:14,812 --> 00:11:15,812
Get some sleep.

226
00:11:16,979 --> 00:11:17,979
Okay.

227
00:11:30,565 --> 00:11:32,112
That little brat!

228
00:11:33,891 --> 00:11:35,772
The person you're calling
is unavailable...

229
00:11:36,471 --> 00:11:37,848
She's not answering.

230
00:11:39,031 --> 00:11:41,398
I don't get a single day of peace!

231
00:11:47,393 --> 00:11:48,525
Ji Hu.

232
00:11:51,618 --> 00:11:53,556
We've waited this long.
Let's give her a little more time.

233
00:11:53,685 --> 00:11:56,324
Sometimes a little trip
is better than staying home.

234
00:11:56,418 --> 00:11:58,710
She's going on a trip
and leaving divorce papers behind?

235
00:11:58,932 --> 00:12:00,199
Then just don't sign the papers.

236
00:12:01,905 --> 00:12:03,880
- Where are the papers?
- I don't know.

237
00:12:04,391 --> 00:12:05,615
Maybe your mom has them.

238
00:12:10,066 --> 00:12:12,466
What a relief. I feel so much lighter.

239
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:15,900
Mom.

240
00:12:16,598 --> 00:12:17,976
You startled me.

241
00:12:18,816 --> 00:12:19,816
Did you find her?

242
00:12:20,075 --> 00:12:21,075
No.

243
00:12:21,645 --> 00:12:23,639
I told you. Leave her alone.

244
00:12:24,018 --> 00:12:25,256
Where are the divorce papers?

245
00:12:26,794 --> 00:12:27,794
Why?

246
00:12:27,795 --> 00:12:28,808
I'll keep them.

247
00:12:29,042 --> 00:12:30,502
I just tore them up.

248
00:12:31,298 --> 00:12:32,659
Why would you want to keep them?

249
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:33,660
You threw them away?

250
00:12:34,038 --> 00:12:35,038
Of course.

251
00:12:35,830 --> 00:12:36,830
Good.

252
00:12:51,831 --> 00:12:53,340
(Application for Divorce
by Mutual Consent)

253
00:13:29,071 --> 00:13:31,120
I thought she might have left
something behind.

254
00:13:32,392 --> 00:13:34,154
There must be something about me
in there too.

255
00:13:34,249 --> 00:13:35,376
Of course there is.

256
00:13:36,266 --> 00:13:37,809
She went on and on about it.

257
00:13:38,632 --> 00:13:40,286
Ji Hu doesn't know a thing.

258
00:13:40,958 --> 00:13:42,978
From now on, it's all up to you.

259
00:13:46,665 --> 00:13:48,413
You said you couldn't do it,

260
00:13:48,415 --> 00:13:49,985
but you came through in the end.

261
00:13:50,152 --> 00:13:54,015
What on earth did you do to Ji Ni
to make her so downhearted...

262
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:57,598
that she signed the divorce papers
without a fight?

263
00:13:59,065 --> 00:14:00,458
I didn't say much.

264
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:02,314
Playing innocent.

265
00:14:03,691 --> 00:14:07,265
Anyway, be good to Ji Hu.

266
00:14:08,065 --> 00:14:11,468
When someone's vulnerable,
kindness can open their heart.

267
00:14:11,555 --> 00:14:12,555
Okay?

268
00:14:12,772 --> 00:14:14,156
It's not working yet.

269
00:14:14,851 --> 00:14:16,307
You know what Ji Hu is going through.

270
00:14:16,365 --> 00:14:17,734
After their friend leaves,

271
00:14:18,142 --> 00:14:20,205
plenty of women marry...

272
00:14:20,206 --> 00:14:21,625
the lonely husband she left behind.

273
00:14:21,698 --> 00:14:23,218
That's common in novels, isn't it?

274
00:14:24,158 --> 00:14:25,911
You're not the only one doing it.

275
00:14:26,218 --> 00:14:30,167
Don't worry.
Take your time, but don't let up.

276
00:14:30,999 --> 00:14:32,991
Keep going after Ji Hu, okay?

277
00:14:33,654 --> 00:14:34,654
Okay.

278
00:14:34,911 --> 00:14:36,712
I've come this far. I'll do my best.

279
00:14:36,819 --> 00:14:37,911
That's the spirit.

280
00:14:39,438 --> 00:14:40,938
Ji Ni is out of the picture now.

281
00:14:41,558 --> 00:14:44,791
Ji Hu belongs to me.
I'm giving you permission.

282
00:14:54,645 --> 00:14:56,078
Is that Ji Ni? Answer it.

283
00:14:59,639 --> 00:15:00,648
Hello?

284
00:15:00,663 --> 00:15:02,556
Jung A, where are you?

285
00:15:02,732 --> 00:15:04,645
Is that you, ma'am?

286
00:15:06,252 --> 00:15:08,007
I only heard about it last night too.

287
00:15:09,291 --> 00:15:10,291
Yes.

288
00:15:12,865 --> 00:15:14,065
It's Ji Ni's mom.

289
00:15:14,101 --> 00:15:15,101
Go ahead.

290
00:15:15,898 --> 00:15:17,197
That mistress...

291
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:19,939
is finally scrambling
to find her daughter.

292
00:15:20,272 --> 00:15:22,640
She has no idea her daughter
is paying the price for her.

293
00:15:23,363 --> 00:15:24,363
Excuse me.

294
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:26,220
Yes?

295
00:15:27,042 --> 00:15:28,042
Can I help you find something?

296
00:15:29,144 --> 00:15:32,103
A lot of people around me
have been playing park golf lately.

297
00:15:32,128 --> 00:15:33,773
I just started playing too.

298
00:15:33,798 --> 00:15:36,155
But walking on grass
and dirt paths for so long...

299
00:15:36,179 --> 00:15:38,179
makes my feet tire easily.

300
00:15:38,658 --> 00:15:41,369
Someone recommended your shoes,
so I came to take a look.

301
00:15:41,492 --> 00:15:42,492
Which ones would you recommend?

302
00:15:42,516 --> 00:15:44,704
Well, you've come to the right place.

303
00:15:44,952 --> 00:15:47,943
We just got a new line
of park golf shoes in.

304
00:15:48,113 --> 00:15:49,733
Aren't they pretty? Try them on.

305
00:15:52,632 --> 00:15:54,318
They're so pretty.

306
00:15:54,565 --> 00:15:55,705
- Aren't they?
- Yes.

307
00:15:55,730 --> 00:15:58,797
Our park golf shoes
provide great stability,

308
00:15:58,967 --> 00:16:01,957
so they're comfortable to wear
while playing.

309
00:16:02,338 --> 00:16:05,018
They're also easy on your feet
during long walks.

310
00:16:05,492 --> 00:16:08,622
They're great for everyday wear too.

311
00:16:08,646 --> 00:16:09,646
Pretty, right?

312
00:16:09,745 --> 00:16:10,907
They're so pretty.

313
00:16:10,932 --> 00:16:12,433
And they're comfortable too.

314
00:16:12,457 --> 00:16:13,513
Right?

315
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:15,900
Is that all?

316
00:16:16,092 --> 00:16:18,012
She asked you to look after Ji Hu?

317
00:16:18,505 --> 00:16:20,533
Does that even make sense?

318
00:16:20,998 --> 00:16:23,046
I guess it's because we're friends.

319
00:16:23,305 --> 00:16:24,906
Tae O heard it too.

320
00:16:25,472 --> 00:16:27,685
Didn't she leave a letter or anything?

321
00:16:28,407 --> 00:16:30,131
I haven't heard anything about that.

322
00:16:31,018 --> 00:16:32,894
She'd never do something like this.

323
00:16:33,112 --> 00:16:34,581
She wouldn't just agree to a divorce...

324
00:16:35,225 --> 00:16:36,526
It makes no sense.

325
00:16:37,052 --> 00:16:40,858
Someone must've pressured her
or tricked her. Something's going on.

326
00:16:40,992 --> 00:16:42,176
Look into it for me.

327
00:16:42,325 --> 00:16:44,563
I can't just come and go from that house,

328
00:16:44,587 --> 00:16:46,963
and Yeong Ju isn't there now, either.

329
00:16:47,404 --> 00:16:49,661
Okay. I'll let you know
if I find anything.

330
00:16:50,184 --> 00:16:52,844
If you notice anything suspicious,

331
00:16:52,868 --> 00:16:55,883
or manage to reach Ji Ni,
tell me right away.

332
00:16:56,624 --> 00:16:57,795
Okay, I will.

333
00:16:59,349 --> 00:17:00,349
Ji Ni...

334
00:17:12,218 --> 00:17:13,218
Sun Kyung?

335
00:17:13,295 --> 00:17:14,295
Yeah.

336
00:17:14,425 --> 00:17:16,484
I wanted to ask Jung A if Sun Kyung...

337
00:17:16,485 --> 00:17:18,131
had been giving Ji Ni a hard time,

338
00:17:18,530 --> 00:17:21,417
but Ji Ni isn't the type
to share every little detail,

339
00:17:21,418 --> 00:17:22,896
so I came to you, Sa Bin.

340
00:17:23,078 --> 00:17:25,719
You live under the same roof,
so you must see what's going on.

341
00:17:25,786 --> 00:17:27,270
Whether she's comfortable or not.

342
00:17:27,328 --> 00:17:30,769
I've been staying in Seo Chon lately,
so I wouldn't know.

343
00:17:32,125 --> 00:17:34,341
Ji Ni hasn't done anything wrong.

344
00:17:34,893 --> 00:17:38,628
How badly must they have treated her
to make her give up on her own?

345
00:17:38,652 --> 00:17:40,562
I even said I'd cut ties with her.

346
00:17:41,664 --> 00:17:45,152
Her only mistake was being born to me.
That's all she's ever done wrong.

347
00:17:45,176 --> 00:17:46,176
I know.

348
00:17:46,559 --> 00:17:47,559
But...

349
00:17:47,935 --> 00:17:50,628
our whole family treated her well.

350
00:17:51,231 --> 00:17:54,253
If it weren't for the Lee Cheol incident,
none of this would have happened.

351
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:56,883
So it's my fault again.

352
00:17:58,203 --> 00:17:59,665
What did Joong Bin say?

353
00:18:00,005 --> 00:18:02,610
He's not really going
to file for divorce, is he?

354
00:18:02,612 --> 00:18:04,885
Of course not. He won't.

355
00:18:05,042 --> 00:18:07,007
Ji Hu wouldn't do that. Trust me.

356
00:18:07,289 --> 00:18:10,258
Right. That's my only hope.

357
00:18:11,375 --> 00:18:12,375
Thanks.

358
00:18:14,491 --> 00:18:15,491
Sa Bin.

359
00:18:16,659 --> 00:18:17,760
Ji Ni...

360
00:18:18,391 --> 00:18:20,205
isn't thinking of doing something bad
again, is she?

361
00:18:20,230 --> 00:18:21,765
Of course not.

362
00:18:22,164 --> 00:18:24,959
She's going through a lot
and just needed to get out for a while.

363
00:18:25,605 --> 00:18:29,900
Maestro, don't just leave.
You should get some acupuncture...

364
00:18:29,901 --> 00:18:32,318
and have some medicine prescribed too.
You look terrible.

365
00:18:32,343 --> 00:18:34,678
No, forget the acupuncture.

366
00:18:34,876 --> 00:18:36,798
Could I borrow your car?

367
00:18:36,972 --> 00:18:39,275
I want to look around some places
that come to mind.

368
00:18:43,752 --> 00:18:45,193
I've already explained everything.

369
00:18:45,685 --> 00:18:47,646
- If you need documents, submit these.
- Okay.

370
00:18:48,625 --> 00:18:49,625
Search everywhere.

371
00:18:50,165 --> 00:18:51,931
Planes, trains, buses, islands, the sea.

372
00:18:52,458 --> 00:18:54,088
Search every place you can reach.

373
00:18:55,298 --> 00:18:58,007
Even the ferries departing from Incheon.

374
00:18:58,844 --> 00:19:00,247
Would she really take a ferry?

375
00:19:01,078 --> 00:19:02,988
Anyway, understood.
I'll search everywhere.

376
00:19:03,771 --> 00:19:04,933
You have to find her.

377
00:19:27,112 --> 00:19:29,300
That smells good.

378
00:19:29,411 --> 00:19:31,013
Ma'am, could you taste it for me?

379
00:19:31,015 --> 00:19:32,248
- Should I?
- Yes.

380
00:19:36,303 --> 00:19:38,387
- This is delicious.
- Really?

381
00:19:39,509 --> 00:19:41,340
How are you so good at seasoning food?

382
00:19:41,365 --> 00:19:42,387
- Thank you.
- You should try some too.

383
00:19:42,412 --> 00:19:43,412
Okay.

384
00:19:43,762 --> 00:19:45,569
- Are you heading inside?
- Yeah.

385
00:19:46,398 --> 00:19:47,908
Move the rest quickly.

386
00:19:47,932 --> 00:19:48,932
(One Week Later)

387
00:20:05,485 --> 00:20:07,467
Looks like you're getting
the hang of the work.

388
00:20:07,951 --> 00:20:09,791
Yes.

389
00:20:09,878 --> 00:20:11,286
I was pretty clumsy at first, wasn't I?

390
00:20:11,395 --> 00:20:12,577
Everyone starts that way.

391
00:20:12,679 --> 00:20:14,154
How's the place you're staying?

392
00:20:14,891 --> 00:20:15,891
It's fine.

393
00:20:15,916 --> 00:20:17,500
There aren't many Koreans here.

394
00:20:17,545 --> 00:20:19,540
But everyone speaks Korean well, right?

395
00:20:20,042 --> 00:20:22,172
Yes. Everyone's been very kind.

396
00:20:22,715 --> 00:20:24,042
Thank you.

397
00:20:27,671 --> 00:20:29,183
Snack break!

398
00:20:29,379 --> 00:20:30,800
It's break time.

399
00:20:32,570 --> 00:20:34,126
Come get some snacks!

400
00:20:34,225 --> 00:20:35,331
- Okay.
- Come over here.

401
00:20:35,355 --> 00:20:36,436
Enjoy.

402
00:20:36,461 --> 00:20:39,015
- Thanks.
- Sit here.

403
00:20:40,112 --> 00:20:43,284
Let's take a break.

404
00:20:43,389 --> 00:20:45,056
Thank you.

405
00:20:47,885 --> 00:20:49,670
I guess you've never done
this kind of work before.

406
00:20:49,872 --> 00:20:50,930
What did you do before?

407
00:20:51,585 --> 00:20:52,735
Well...

408
00:20:53,726 --> 00:20:54,726
Just...

409
00:20:54,750 --> 00:20:55,945
Are you married?

410
00:20:56,911 --> 00:20:57,911
Yes.

411
00:20:58,492 --> 00:20:59,596
Really?

412
00:20:59,621 --> 00:21:01,657
Is it okay for you
to live apart like this?

413
00:21:02,338 --> 00:21:04,562
We're working hard to save up for a house.

414
00:21:04,711 --> 00:21:06,994
You two sound like a hardworking couple.

415
00:21:07,178 --> 00:21:09,560
There aren't many places
that pay this well per day.

416
00:21:09,832 --> 00:21:11,993
You want to be paid in cash like them?

417
00:21:12,930 --> 00:21:13,930
Yes.

418
00:21:14,978 --> 00:21:17,254
Come back to pick cabbages
after the apple harvest.

419
00:21:17,472 --> 00:21:19,377
We'll be harvesting cabbages in Danyang.

420
00:21:19,525 --> 00:21:21,570
Just let me join you. I'll work hard.

421
00:21:23,051 --> 00:21:24,978
What does your husband do? Is he handsome?

422
00:21:25,014 --> 00:21:27,928
She's so pretty.
She must've picked a handsome guy.

423
00:21:28,709 --> 00:21:31,829
Yes. He's handsome and plays
the piano well. That's why I chose him.

424
00:21:31,853 --> 00:21:33,573
She says he's handsome.

425
00:21:34,056 --> 00:21:35,728
Looks really do matter in a man.

426
00:21:52,532 --> 00:21:54,033
Hello.

427
00:21:54,955 --> 00:21:56,191
Hello.

428
00:22:17,318 --> 00:22:18,546
Ji Hu.

429
00:22:20,049 --> 00:22:21,712
I hope you're doing okay.

430
00:22:23,571 --> 00:22:25,137
You have to be okay.

431
00:22:27,935 --> 00:22:28,996
Mom...

432
00:22:40,210 --> 00:22:41,512
- Nothing at all?
- No.

433
00:22:41,763 --> 00:22:43,649
She hasn't used her cards,
and her phone is off.

434
00:22:43,918 --> 00:22:45,271
How can this be?

435
00:22:45,876 --> 00:22:47,271
But...

436
00:22:47,756 --> 00:22:49,886
- What is it?
- Lee Cheol has been caught.

437
00:22:50,158 --> 00:22:52,039
He was caught trying to sneak into China.

438
00:22:52,572 --> 00:22:54,445
The captain of the boat he'd asked
to smuggle him out...

439
00:22:54,689 --> 00:22:56,785
- turned out to be Captain Kim.
- Captain Kim?

440
00:22:57,012 --> 00:22:58,277
Captain Kim Yeong Cheol?

441
00:22:58,301 --> 00:22:59,301
Yes.

442
00:22:59,892 --> 00:23:02,840
Captain Kim knew Lee Cheol was wanted.

443
00:23:02,865 --> 00:23:05,625
So he reported him to the police
before setting sail for China.

444
00:23:05,732 --> 00:23:06,959
He's being questioned now.

445
00:23:06,983 --> 00:23:09,632
Good. That's a relief.

446
00:23:11,997 --> 00:23:13,664
Hello.

447
00:23:13,665 --> 00:23:14,887
Hello.

448
00:23:17,238 --> 00:23:18,238
What brings you here?

449
00:23:18,531 --> 00:23:20,433
Have a seat.

450
00:23:20,832 --> 00:23:22,352
What do you mean, what brings her here?

451
00:23:22,718 --> 00:23:24,599
Jung A is Ji Hu's friend.

452
00:23:25,198 --> 00:23:28,522
Ji Hu hasn't been looking well lately,
so she came to cheer him up.

453
00:23:28,638 --> 00:23:30,015
And have dinner with us.

454
00:23:31,152 --> 00:23:32,303
Jung A, what do you like to eat?

455
00:23:32,505 --> 00:23:34,100
I'll eat anything.

456
00:23:35,259 --> 00:23:36,873
Send Ji Hu a message
and ask when he'll be home.

457
00:23:36,897 --> 00:23:37,897
Okay.

458
00:24:02,131 --> 00:24:03,131
Honey.

459
00:24:04,073 --> 00:24:05,747
You can find Ji Ni, can't you?

460
00:24:05,772 --> 00:24:06,940
You're just not looking, right?

461
00:24:07,758 --> 00:24:10,688
There you go again,
accusing me of something I didn't do.

462
00:24:10,971 --> 00:24:12,742
I really can't find her.

463
00:24:13,392 --> 00:24:15,763
There are too many suspicious people.

464
00:24:16,640 --> 00:24:17,707
Who else is suspicious?

465
00:24:17,708 --> 00:24:20,549
I think the ones who made Ji Ni leave...

466
00:24:22,165 --> 00:24:24,692
are those two over there.
That's my gut feeling.

467
00:24:25,392 --> 00:24:27,160
I'm thinking of telling Ji Hu.

468
00:24:28,513 --> 00:24:31,221
Do you want to get us into trouble?
Keep your mouth shut.

469
00:24:31,246 --> 00:24:32,763
It's none of our business.

470
00:24:41,997 --> 00:24:43,901
Should I discuss it with Yeong Ju?

471
00:25:18,478 --> 00:25:19,478
Aren't you going home?

472
00:25:21,358 --> 00:25:22,551
Have something to eat.

473
00:25:22,576 --> 00:25:24,518
You need your strength to keep waiting.

474
00:25:24,812 --> 00:25:25,884
You go ahead.

475
00:25:27,418 --> 00:25:28,524
What's the point of going home?

476
00:25:29,931 --> 00:25:31,124
What if...

477
00:25:31,785 --> 00:25:33,462
Ji Ni never comes back?

478
00:25:34,392 --> 00:25:35,849
Will you agree to the divorce?

479
00:25:36,693 --> 00:25:37,693
Are you crazy?

480
00:25:41,152 --> 00:25:42,499
Honestly, I'm not sure.

481
00:25:44,272 --> 00:25:46,665
I don't know what Ji Ni really wants.

482
00:25:48,591 --> 00:25:50,634
If she's hidden so well
that even Lieutenant No can't find her,

483
00:25:51,626 --> 00:25:53,660
maybe she really wants to leave me.

484
00:26:00,012 --> 00:26:01,597
I don't know if I should say this, but...

485
00:26:02,701 --> 00:26:04,784
do you know who saw Ji Ni last?

486
00:26:06,418 --> 00:26:07,981
Your mom and Jung A.

487
00:26:09,905 --> 00:26:12,179
I'm not saying
that means anything, though.

488
00:26:12,686 --> 00:26:13,906
I don't know.

489
00:26:14,452 --> 00:26:16,072
I don't even know what I'm saying anymore.

490
00:26:16,097 --> 00:26:18,617
Are you saying Mom
and Jung A know something?

491
00:26:19,245 --> 00:26:20,385
Just speak freely.

492
00:26:21,001 --> 00:26:23,540
It's just that your mom...

493
00:26:23,936 --> 00:26:25,986
definitely hated Ji Ni,

494
00:26:26,356 --> 00:26:27,806
and Jung A liked you.

495
00:26:29,190 --> 00:26:31,205
Your mom and Jung A were also close.

496
00:26:31,918 --> 00:26:32,918
But...

497
00:26:33,322 --> 00:26:35,361
haven't you noticed Jung A acting strange?

498
00:26:36,738 --> 00:26:37,955
I don't know.

499
00:26:38,221 --> 00:26:40,266
Hey, who is Jung A? She's Ji Ni's friend.

500
00:26:40,380 --> 00:26:41,990
Have you seen Jung A looking for Ji Ni?

501
00:26:42,145 --> 00:26:43,230
I haven't.

502
00:26:43,878 --> 00:26:45,391
Is this how Jung A would normally act?

503
00:26:48,045 --> 00:26:49,443
Something's definitely going on.

504
00:26:49,691 --> 00:26:50,891
I just don't know what.

505
00:26:56,404 --> 00:26:58,457
I guess these are really popular lately.

506
00:26:58,482 --> 00:27:00,313
That's right.
I've been seeing these a lot.

507
00:27:00,792 --> 00:27:03,046
That's the scent I always smell on you.

508
00:27:03,322 --> 00:27:04,828
- That's right.
- It smells so nice.

509
00:27:04,852 --> 00:27:05,955
Doesn't it?

510
00:27:06,425 --> 00:27:07,425
Ji Hu.

511
00:27:07,936 --> 00:27:08,975
Ji Hu, you're here?

512
00:27:09,331 --> 00:27:10,331
You come here a lot.

513
00:27:10,812 --> 00:27:12,351
I invited her.

514
00:27:12,692 --> 00:27:15,212
The house is so gloomy.
I wanted to hear some laughter.

515
00:27:15,851 --> 00:27:18,167
I was just about to leave anyway.

516
00:27:19,095 --> 00:27:21,751
No, Jung A. Stay for dinner.

517
00:27:22,305 --> 00:27:25,634
You have no idea
how much she's helped me at the store.

518
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:28,367
What would you like to eat?

519
00:27:28,392 --> 00:27:30,043
Want some of those glass noodles
you had last time?

520
00:27:30,068 --> 00:27:31,583
I'd like that too.

521
00:27:35,145 --> 00:27:36,145
What is it?

522
00:27:36,922 --> 00:27:37,922
Nothing.

523
00:27:39,159 --> 00:27:41,257
Mom, can I borrow your phone?

524
00:27:41,578 --> 00:27:43,084
My phone's been acting up
since this afternoon.

525
00:27:43,108 --> 00:27:44,241
My phone?

526
00:27:44,266 --> 00:27:46,135
It's in the bedroom. The master bedroom.

527
00:27:47,185 --> 00:27:48,867
Jung A, stay and eat before you go.

528
00:27:51,604 --> 00:27:52,604
Let's go.

529
00:28:45,952 --> 00:28:49,245
(Family Register)

530
00:28:49,303 --> 00:28:51,186
Why do you keep coming here when Ji Ni
isn't even around? Aren't you her friend?

531
00:28:51,218 --> 00:28:53,759
It's not like Ji Ni left because of me.
Why are you taking it out on me?

532
00:28:53,783 --> 00:28:55,952
- You're making me uncomfortable.
- Your wife ghosted you and divorced you.

533
00:28:55,976 --> 00:28:58,245
- Mom. Seriously!
- Jung A got medicine for Ji Hu? Why?

534
00:28:58,270 --> 00:29:00,913
She's a loyal friend, just like you.

535
00:29:00,937 --> 00:29:02,956
Do you think Jung A would make a move
on her friend's husband like you did?

536
